  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "need",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "The blank. Measure it. If it differs by more than 0.5 mm in any dimension, change the job and regenerate — do not run this file.",
          "value": "100 × 60 × 12 mm softwood",
        },
        {
          "text": "The cutter — 1 mm flat end (assumed).",
          "value": "⌀ 1 mm cutting",
        },
        {
          "record": "flute length (mm) / stick-out (mm)",
          "text": "Record the cutter's flute length and its stick-out from the collet.",
        },
        {
          "text": "The Z1 low-profile vise, and the wired probe that ships with the machine — a mechanical touch tip, so it triggers on PLA (measured 2026-10-08, 0.001 mm). The 3D Probe stays in reserve.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Depth margins — how far every floor stays clear of a plane: a void’s ceiling, the colour split. Recommended for this blank: 0.2 mm — the wired probe adds 0.001 mm; flatness unknown: no number for the dome.",
          "value": "0.2 mm boundary margin · the house default · no print stated: a void’s ceiling keeps the job’s minimum floor, 1 mm",
        },
        {
          "text": "Under-surface void — Magnet pocket. The blank is only 2 mm thick over it: do not cut through.",
          "value": "deepest cut 1 mm",
        },
      ],
      "title": "1 · What you need",
    },
    {
      "id": "mount",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Remove the MDF wasteboard. Seat the vise on its two locating pins; fasten with six M5×20 screws.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "The fixed jaw is on the left.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
      ],
      "title": "2 · Mount the vise",
    },
    {
      "id": "load",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "The blank's length runs left–right between the jaws. The face to be engraved is up.",
          "value": "100 mm",
        },
        {
          "record": "measured stock proud (mm)",
          "text": "The top face must stand 4 mm above the jaw tops. Record the measured value. No cut on this job sweeps over a jaw, so there is no stop threshold to check.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Push the blank's front edge to where the file expects it: the front edge is 10 mm behind the front of the jaws.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Tighten. Check the blank does not rock.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "3 · Load the blank",
    },
    {
      "id": "cutter",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Fit the cutter with its collar. Run tool-length calibration from Studio (M491).",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not skip this because the program contains T1 M6. If the machine already believes tool 1 is fitted, that line does nothing.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
      ],
      "title": "4 · Fit the cutter and measure its length",
    },
    {
      "id": "origin",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "The vise already references X and rotation to within ±0.05 mm, before any touch.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Touch 1 of 3: the front edge — the one nearest you, about 25 mm along it from the left end — this gives position and rotation.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Touch 2 of 3: the front edge — the one nearest you, about 75 mm along it from the left end — this gives rotation.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Touch 3 of 3: the right edge — the one against the moving jaw, at about its middle, 30 mm from the front end — this gives X.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Z0: the blank's top face — probe it, or touch off on it.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "X0 Y0 Z0 is the top-front-left corner of the blank. That leaves the work origin within ±0.02 mm in X and Y and ±0.02° in rotation. Move there and check by eye before going on.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Rotation is measured, and a static .nc cannot compensate it (Smoothieware has no variables, §7.3 / #187 item 1): apply it in Studio's dialogs, or re-post with the rotation baked into the geometry",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Z is always probed on the engraved face (§7.2): no fixture can supply it",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "OPTIONAL, BEFORE THE FIRST CUT — check where the blank really is, with the wired probe. It is Z-only, so it cannot touch a side: it finds an edge by touching DOWN at points across it and watching where the reading changes. 4 edges, 4 touches each, a few minutes, one tool change. Skip this if this is the blank you have just set the origin against.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Fit the probe and touch off ONCE on the blank’s top face, near the middle (M491 for the probe’s own length). Every reading below is a change from this one, so its Z is the zero depth to compare against.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Set the touch-off’s travel limit — the cap — before the first edge touch:",
          "unverified": "#208",
          "value": "cap 5 mm below the reference",
        },
        {
          "record": "X where the reading stops being the blank (mm)",
          "text": "Check the left edge — the one against the fixed jaw — at the middle of the blank’s width. Touch down at 3.5 and 1.5 mm inside (the blank’s own top), at 1.2 mm outside (the blank’s edge itself — the tip is over the corner), and at 3.5 mm outside (off the blank and lower — the jaw’s top, or whatever is under the tip).",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "record": "X where the reading stops being the blank (mm)",
          "text": "Check the right edge — the one against the moving jaw — at the middle of the blank’s width. Touch down at 3.5 and 1.5 mm inside (the blank’s own top), at 1.2 mm outside (the blank’s edge itself — the tip is over the corner), and at 3.5 mm outside (off the blank and lower — the jaw’s top, or whatever is under the tip).",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "record": "Y where the reading stops being the blank (mm)",
          "text": "Check the front edge — the one nearest you — at the middle of the blank’s length. Touch down at 3.5 and 1.5 mm inside (the blank’s own top), at 1.2 mm outside (the blank’s edge itself — the tip is over the corner), and at 3.5 mm outside (nothing at all: the tip stops on its travel cap) — no jaw reaches under the tip past that edge, so a miss there is the expected reading, not a fault.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "record": "Y where the reading stops being the blank (mm)",
          "text": "Check the back edge — the one furthest from you — at the middle of the blank’s length. Touch down at 3.5 and 1.5 mm inside (the blank’s own top), at 1.2 mm outside (the blank’s edge itself — the tip is over the corner), and at 3.5 mm outside (nothing at all: the tip stops on its travel cap) — no jaw reaches under the tip past that edge, so a miss there is the expected reading, not a fault.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "text": "Reading the depths: within 0.38 mm of the reference is the blank’s own top, 3.95 mm or more below it is off the blank, and between the two the tip is on the edge itself. The reading leaves the blank about 0.998 mm BEFORE the edge, so measure back 0.998 mm from where it changed: that is where the edge is. If the change comes at the inside touch nearest the edge, bisect — halve the gap, touch the middle, keep the two readings that straddle it — until the two are 1 mm apart.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
        {
          "record": "edge that is out, and by how much (mm)",
          "text": "Compare with the file: the edges should lie where it says they do — X = 0 and X = 100 for the left and right, Y = 0 and Y = 60 for the front and back — after the 0.998 mm above is taken off. More than the job’s own margin out, and the blank has moved: re-clamp it, or set the origin from the measured position. Do not cut until the two agree.",
          "unverified": "#208",
          "value": "allowed 1 mm",
        },
        {
          "text": "Put the CUTTER back and measure its length again (M491): the probe and the cutter are different tools, and every Z in the program is the cutter’s.",
          "unverified": "#208",
        },
      ],
      "title": "5 · Set the work origin",
    },
    {
      "id": "dry-run",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Load Untitled-engrave-job-frame.nc and run it. The cutter traces the job's outline in the air, 20 mm above the work — no Z offset to set. Watch that the trace stays over the blank and clear of the jaws.",
          "value": "20 mm above the work",
        },
        {
          "text": "If the trace is not where the job should land, stop and change the job. Otherwise load Untitled-engrave-job.nc and cut.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "6 · Dry run",
    },
    {
      "id": "cut",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Spindle, feed, plunge, passes and step-down. Vacuum on.",
          "value": "12000 RPM · 500 mm/min feed · 200 mm/min plunge · 2 × 0.5 mm passes · 0.45 mm step-over",
        },
        {
          "text": "Engrave "CASE"",
          "value": "2 mm deep",
        },
        {
          "text": "Engrave "MAKER" — over "Magnet pocket", only 2 mm of material (deepest cut there 1 mm)",
          "value": "1 mm deep",
        },
        {
          "text": "Engrave "first chips"",
          "value": "0.5 mm deep",
        },
        {
          "text": "Stay at the machine. Stop it if the sound changes, the blank moves, or the cutter loads up.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "7 · Cut",
    },
    {
      "id": "warnings",
      "steps": [
        {
          "bold": true,
          "text": "Vise dimensions are unmeasured defaults (#208); collisions cannot be trusted yet.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Checked: the tool against the stock and the modelled fixture (Vise fixed jaw (left), Vise moving jaw (right)).",
        },
        {
          "text": "Not checked: the spindle body, head and gantry; anything on the bed other than the declared stock, workholding and sacrificial material.",
        },
        {
          "text": "The modelled fixture is a shipped default, not a measurement.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "8 · Warnings carried from the app",
    },
    {
      "id": "record",
      "steps": [
        {
          "record": "measured depth (mm)",
          "text": "Measured floor depth — Engrave "CASE"",
        },
        {
          "record": "measured depth (mm)",
          "text": "Measured floor depth — Engrave "MAKER"",
        },
        {
          "record": "measured depth (mm)",
          "text": "Measured floor depth — Engrave "first chips"",
        },
        {
          "record": "yes / no",
          "text": "Is the text legible?",
        },
        {
          "record": "clean / fuzzy / burnt",
          "text": "Surface finish",
        },
        {
          "record": "notes",
          "text": "Anything that went wrong",
        },
      ],
      "title": "9 · Record afterwards",
    },
  ],
}
`;

